# BurnhopeEngine Rules & Architectural Manifesto

Be decisive, thorough, and principled. Build robust engine systems from the ground up. Never write ad-hoc glue code or one-off workarounds when a fundamental engine primitive is missing or broken.

- CORE MODULARITY & SINGLE RESPONSIBILITY: The engine core consists of dedicated, single-purpose foundation modules (Input System, Memory Allocators, Draw Dispatcher, Scissor & Viewport State, Text & Glyph Pipeline, Asset Streaming). Every subsystem does exactly one job and does it reliably.
- COMPOSITION OVER DUPLICATION (DRY AT ALL LAYERS): High-level systems (UI panels, File Explorer, Scene View, Render Passes) must NEVER implement their own private versions of low-level logic (e.g. ad-hoc hit-testing, private mouse tracking, manual buffer packing, custom scissor handling). They strictly compose existing core primitives.
- SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH: If an architectural behavior is needed in more than one place, extract it into its dedicated core module. If a bug occurs, fix it once in the root module so every dependent engine system immediately inherits the correct behavior.
- ROOT CAUSE FIRST: Freely trace issues down through the layers (composite widget -> base primitives -> Canvas -> RHI -> Vulkan pipeline). Never patch a symptom on the surface when the underlying engine module is faulty.
- MANDATORY BUILD & TEST: After making edits, ALWAYS verify both targets:
  `cmake --build build-core --target BurnhopeTest BurnhopeEngine -j && ./build-core/BurnhopeTest`
  Task is COMPLETE ONLY if BOTH targets compile cleanly and all unit tests pass.
- NO TERMINAL SPAM: Do not run `git diff` or cat whole files into chat via shell. Output clear, direct code modifications.

## 1. Target Platforms & Scope
- **Target**: High-performance Desktop PC ONLY (Linux & Windows x86_64 with AVX2).
- **STRICTLY BANNED**: ARM, Android, iOS, WebAssembly, macOS, and any mobile/low-end embedded workarounds. Zero overhead for non-desktop architectures.
- **Vision**: Modern clean DOD engine outperforming Unreal Engine / Source 2 in latency, memory footprint, and CPU overhead. Qt-level UI capability with zero OOP baggage.

## 2. Core Architecture, C++26 & Data-Oriented Design
- **Language**: Strict C++26. Pure Data-Oriented Design (DOD) with Struct-of-Arrays (SoA).
- **Core Decoupling**: `core/` is completely standalone. Foundation modules in `core/` have zero knowledge of higher layers and NEVER reference `engine/`, `demo/`, or `old/`.
- **ECS (Flecs)**: Query archetype column pointers (`flecs::column<T>`). NEVER call `entity.get<T>()` / `try_get<T>()` in hot loops.
- **Hot-Path Allocations**: ZERO heap allocations in `Tick`, `Layout`, `Emit`, `Draw`. NO `malloc`, `new`, `std::string`, `push_back` reallocations, or `std::make_shared`. Use bump allocators, ring buffers, or `FrameArena`.
- **POD Invariants**: All GPU and UI data must be trivially copyable POD types (`sizeof % 16 == 0`).

## 3. UI Framework & Rendering Architecture
- **Layered Structure**: Base components (Button, Label, Scroll, Icon) sit directly on top of Core Primitives (Input, Canvas, Scissor Manager). High-level compound views (Explorer, Inspector, Tree) only assemble these components.
- **BANNED UI**: Absolutely NO ImGui, NO Qt (`QObject`, MOC, virtual dispatch hierarchies), NO legacy immediate-mode GUI hacks.
- **Draw Submission**: Single `vkCmdDraw` / `vkCmdDrawMeshTasksEXT` call per frame from mapped host-visible SSBO ring buffer.
- **Layout Invariants**: NEVER place `uiSlider` with 100% width in horizontal row next to a label (Yoga collapses box to 0). Stack vertically. Role `Scroll` requires `UiScroll.inner`. Find baked nodes by name.
- NEVER write `s.box` for button, check, or card labels (breaks Yoga alignment); ALWAYS let the label flex fill the control.
- NEVER hardcode virtual slot counts (clips 1440p/4K); ALWAYS `uiVirtualCalc` with a recycled pool capped at `kUiPoolCap` (64).
- NEVER paint widget chrome with raw RGB (light themes stay dark); ALWAYS `paintToken` / `UiToken`.
- **UI Icons & Fonts**: UI icons load from `assets/icons/` into designated photo slots. Tag `-89` draws a static photo tinted by paint rgb; never use `-90` for static icons. Bar menus open on LMB using paint tag `-7`. Base UI font is Inter (`canvasUseFont`).
- **Scissor Discipline**: Every container strictly routes clipping through the core scissor manager so text and geometry never leak into neighboring panels.
- NEVER store File Browser, Calendar, Color Picker, or JSON bytes on UiState (domain state on the core context); ALWAYS `UiFileBrowser`, `UiCalendarComponent`, `UiColorPickerComponent`, and `JsonDocument`. NEVER branch `uiEmit` on paint tags `-70..-78` or `-5` (widget drawing inside the batch); ALWAYS `UiDrawHooks`.

## 4. Vulkan 1.4 & Next-Gen Graphics Pipeline
- **Modern Standards REQUIRED**:
  - GPU-Driven pipeline via Mesh Shaders (`VK_EXT_mesh_shader`, meshlets).
  - Dynamic Rendering (`vkCmdBeginRendering` / `vkCmdEndRendering`) with no render pass boilerplate.
  - Shader Objects (`VK_EXT_shader_object` + `vkCmdBindShadersEXT`).
  - Bindless descriptors via `VK_EXT_descriptor_heap` and Buffer Device Address (BDA).
  - Synchronization2 (`vkCmdPipelineBarrier2`), Timeline Semaphores, Host Image Copy.
  - Lighting & GI: Radiance Cascades (RC), clustered light grids, two-phase GPU Hi-Z culling.
- **BANNED Legacy Vulkan**:
  - NEVER use `VkRenderPass`, `VkFramebuffer`, or runtime `VkPipeline`.
  - NEVER use classic descriptor sets/pools (`VkDescriptorSet`), `vkCmdPipelineBarrier` (v1), or binary fences per pass.
  - NEVER call `vkDeviceWaitIdle` or block CPU fences inside the frame loop.
  - NEVER use `VK_KHR_mesh_shader` (use `VK_EXT_mesh_shader`).
  - NEVER write per-dispatch constants via `vkCmdUpdateBuffer`.
- **Submission Contract**: Scene finishes on color after `LOAD_CLEAR` and signals only `uiSem`. Canvas waits `uiSem`, runs `LOAD`, transitions to `PRESENT_SRC`, and signals present. Scene never calls `swapchainToPresent`.

## 5. Memory Slots & Uniform Invariants
- `GizmoGpu` uniform MUST be 320 bytes (multiple of 64).
- `FrameView` is 384 bytes (binding 0). `FrameSun` is 1920 bytes (binding 49, slot `HeapBuf::Sun`). Slider blocks: bindings 50–57 (64 bytes each).
- Canvas primitives strictly own buffer slot 22 (`kUiDescPrims`). Font is 661; UI photos are 662–669. NEVER overwrite slot 22 with render passes (RC hash uses slot 18).
- Shared shader math lives exclusively in `engine/shader/core/` and `camera.slang`. Never duplicate math across passes.

## 6. Self-Maintenance Protocol
- When resolving a bug, banning an API, or adopting a modern pattern, append it directly as a single-line bullet:
  `- NEVER [banned API/action] (causes [technical failure]); ALWAYS [modern alternative] [exact slots/bytes/alignment].`
- Keep exact technical contracts only. Keep this file under 160 lines.